{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/533448-threat-null-where-will-it-be-covered","id":533448,"title":"Threat Null! Where will it be covered?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-30T11:42:58-07:00","id":533448,"title":"Threat Null! Where will it be covered?","content":"I've got the Void Engineers PDF and the new Mage 20th, what I want to know is where Null Threat is going to get full, or at least fuller, coverage.<br /> <br /> I also want details on possible Void Engineer Null types, and how to set up recoving Null Threat mages as PCs.<br /> <br /> How to play &quot;space colonists&quot; that survived recent disasters would be good too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-30-2015, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T11:54:38-07:00","id":533475,"title":"","content":"Threat Null is gonna get a section in Technocracy Reloaded, I believe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T12:47:04-07:00","id":533547,"title":"","content":"Yeah I expect that if Threat Null is going to be talked about more it will be in Technocracy Reloaded, or maybe if they do an M20 book covering the Umbra and Horizon.<br /> <br /> As for 'recovering' Threat Null members into PCs, I don't think its possible. To begin they've been subjected to Void Adaptation and aren't actually human anymore. Plus given how utterly co-oped they are, especially the Autopolitans and Transhumanity, I don't see any of them coming back from it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T13:37:22-07:00","id":533584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/533448-threat-null-where-will-it-be-covered?p=533547#post533547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for 'recovering' Threat Null members into PCs, I don't think its possible. To begin they've been subjected to Void Adaptation and aren't actually human anymore. Plus given how utterly co-oped they are, especially the Autopolitans and Transhumanity, I don't see any of them coming back from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, this should be classified with becoming a Marauder or going through a Caul. <i>I</i> prefer to declare nothing to be functionally impossible with enough Sphere magick, dedication, study, and intent, but if Marauders and Nephandi are unrecoverable in their current incarnations, neither should Threat Null victims.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-30T20:43:05-07:00","id":533965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/533448-threat-null-where-will-it-be-covered?p=533584#post533584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, this should be classified with becoming a Marauder or going through a Caul. <i>I</i> prefer to declare nothing to be functionally impossible with enough Sphere magick, dedication, study, and intent, but if Marauders and Nephandi are unrecoverable in their current incarnations, neither should Threat Null victims.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If the transition from human to spirit is reversable it does bring back the Archmasters and allows reclaiming horizon realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T03:57:08-07:00","id":534205,"title":"","content":"You know what would be cool? A treath null version of the traditions. I want to see how the traditions would react at seeing their believes twisted into an extremist parody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 05-31-2015, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T22:38:14-07:00","id":536541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Aeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/533448-threat-null-where-will-it-be-covered?p=533584#post533584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO, this should be classified with becoming a Marauder or going through a Caul. <i>I</i> prefer to declare nothing to be functionally impossible with enough Sphere magick, dedication, study, and intent, but if Marauders and Nephandi are unrecoverable in their current incarnations, neither should Threat Null victims.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Once upon a time, I tended to view the Technocracy, Marauders, and Nephandi as representatives of the triple dangers of the three kinds of Quiet. The Technocracy's slide from \u201cevil empire\u201d to &quot;misunderstood rivals&quot; left a vacancy there; and for a while, my inclination was to fill that vacancy with Threat Null. <br /> <br /> Of course, these days I just broaden the concept of \u201cMarauder\u201d so that it's no longer limited to Madness; but hey\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/533448-threat-null-where-will-it-be-covered?p=534205#post534205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what would be cool? A treath null version of the traditions. I want to see how the traditions would react at seeing their believes twisted into an extremist parody.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default88b4-2.html\" target=\"_blank\">Here ya go!</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:10:58-07:00","id":1393002,"title":"","content":"I can't reach the page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:30:16-07:00","id":1393007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/533448-threat-null-where-will-it-be-covered?p=1393002#post1393002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't reach the page.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page seems to be dead but archive.org saved a copy <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20150514235737/http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com:80/default88b4-2.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Weirdly the archived version sometimes turns to black after first loading the page, but here's the OP of that thread:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you haven't read the Void Engineers Convention Book and don't want to be spoiled for the true nature of Threat Null (a secret the VEs keep, and many storytellers may not want to have spoiled at their table), stop reading - because it's pretty implicit here...<br /> <br /> So since Threat Null exists, shouldn't these guys as well? Technocrats weren't the only ones on the wrong side when the Storm hit.<br /> <br /> Now obviously since these threats don't share a paradigmatic belief in &quot;Control&quot;, they aren't held together like Threat Null, which likely contributes them to not being a COLLECTIVE threat in the same way. They're as likely to attack/lure/whatever each other as PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Nirvana: The Self is an illusion. These agents of enlightenment will free you of deception and ignorance. Their light removes all boundary between the consciousness and the external world. Harm to one thing afflicts everything, all hidden truths exposed, emotions and agendas melt together between enemies and friends alike. None meet them and return unchanged, and many never reclaim an individual identity to speak of, becoming part of their egoless light from their gazing third-eyes.<br /> <br /> Archons: Agents of the Source - or so they claim. Messengers and Avengers of Divine Commandments. Deliverers of Terrible Miracles and Divine Judgment. Usually appearing as angelic visions of primal flame.<br /> <br /> Liberalines: Chaotic forces of freedom from all bonds of restraint - be it authority, actual imprisonment, your own moral restraints, or the laws of physics. Rarely does the same one appear the same twice, as bizarre form modification through ecstatic self-mutilation is a norm.<br /> <br /> Moroi: Voormas &amp; his ilk. These macabre liches carry the Maelstrom of the Low Umbra in their wake, and will bring the Underworld to the living and the rest of the Umbra to end the boundary of death all together. [I know this is an inversion of what the Euthanatos actually believe; but the extreme of that (ending the world to turn the Cycle on a cosmic scale) is what the Nephandi already have covered - so the traditional Necromancer shtick of Voormas fits well enough here. Of course Senex is still human and upholds the actual Euthanatos ideals against Voormas]<br /> <br /> Exarchs: &quot;Will-Workers&quot; taken to the megalomaniacal extreme. Would be God-Kings who burn with elemental power, bending the Umbra to their will as personal spirit courts. Regal Exemplars of Hubris and Arete (in the Greek sense) wearing their own manifest authority in crowns of lightning.<br /> <br /> The Pattern: Strange observers, slightly off from normal human, but often still supremely innocuous. The universe is their science experiment. Diversely strange phenomena and their often fatal results are inflicted and studied. Everyone on a void ship switches bodies suddenly. Space warps into an endless loop trapping subway riders inside while their train infinitely accelerates. A spontaneous pregnancy results in a hyper-evolved homo-neandrathalus child. All in the name of science.<br /> <br /> The Sacrifice: Blood-Soaked vassals of nature itself. Animal-skulled heads, antlers, cloaks of sea-brined hands, endless bleeding runes, etc etc mark the chthonic atavists of the Sacrifice. The cycle of nature will be upheld, and the blood of those who would hold themselves apart from its tole (like all human civilization) will grease the turn. <br /> <br /> Singularity: solipsistic utopias exist in the virtual realities of the Digital Web. Like fairy tales of old, one must resist the temptations they offer, and long-since bodiless simulators as well, or disappear into a personal paradise never to return. </div> </div> </div>And in later posts they added<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Left out the Dreamspeakers specifically to parallel the Void Engineers. </div> </div> </div>and<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> face_p0lluti0n on rpg.net had a great idea for twisted Dreamspeakers.<br /> <br /> The Emissaries: Half-human, half-spirit hybrids, they wish to bridge the gap not only between humans and spirits, but to merge the Umbra with Earth, replacing the entire world of physicality with the symbolic mechanics of the deepest Umbral realms. Instead of keeping the peace between humans and spirits as they once did, they find it more effective to simple combine the two. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","user":"JesseM","date":". 05-31-2020, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26184-jessem","name":"JesseM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:43:54-07:00","id":1393009,"title":"","content":"The weird blackout is because web.archive.org blocks access to a given page if there are too many accesses of it in a 15-minute period. <br /> <br /> I'm glad that at least some of the previous forum is still archived in some form, though it only appears to be the first page of each forum from what I can tell. So much good stuff, lost\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T22:57:12-07:00","id":1393011,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much! ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T09:12:17-07:00","id":1393111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/533448-threat-null-where-will-it-be-covered?p=536541#post536541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Once upon a time, I tended to view the Technocracy, Marauders, and Nephandi as representatives of the triple dangers of the three kinds of Quiet. The Technocracy's slide from \u201cevil empire\u201d to &amp;quot;misunderstood rivals&amp;quot; left a vacancy there; and for a while, my inclination was to fill that vacancy with Threat Null.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, I want this expanded. Just imagine static-warped radio transmissions, spam messages full of gibberish and flickering screen glitches that make it past VE surveillance, with an effect similar to the Weaver's Onesong. Cargo cults of half-indoctrinated awakened and unawakened, constructing barely understood eldritch machinery out of flotsam and jetsam, infiltrating and conspiring in the shadows of the other factions, *worshipping* science through arcane techno-rituals and gory body modification(death to videodrome, long live the new flesh)<br /> <br /> Heck, just look at the God-Machine for inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23964-el-barto","name":"El Barto","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-31T11:53:45-07:00","id":1393166,"title":"","content":"I've commented elsewhere that I was disappointed with TR Unit 8. A big part of that is that the section on Threat Null was the most detailed part of it; but it was largely a rehash of what the Void Engineers Convention Book provided. And the three parts that weren't rehashes were uninspired: \u201cThreat Marauder: what if a large contingent of the Union is literally Mad Scientists? Threat Caul: what if the Nephandi have infiltrated the Union? The Sentinels: the Threat Null counterpart to the Void Engineers is indistinguishable from the Void Engineers.\u201d<br /> <br /> I would be more inclined to replace Threat Marauder with Threat Negation: that is, take the basic premise of Quiet running rampant in the Union's ranks; but say that that Quiet leans heavily toward Denial, and that the resulting Marauders are Negation Men. Threat Caul is basically another name for the Technephandi, so I see little point in mentioning them here. <br /> <br /> And instead of Sentinels, I'd rather the Threat Null counterpart to the VEs be Aliens: old-style explorer-type former VEs who have \u201cgone native\u201d and are rarely encountered because they're too busy exploring the depths of the Deep Universe and no longer have any interest in Earth or its affairs. That is, until they realize that Earth's resources are something that they can't survive without, at which point they turn around and become Alien Invaders. <br /> <br /> And as for the other four Conventions, I like El Barto's thoughts: a Threat Null that starts establishing beachheads on Earth might start to look like what he's describing. <br /> <br /> It would make for a good Storyteller's Vault supplement, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T21:49:00-07:00","id":1394237,"title":"","content":"For me, I at once like the idea of the VE's not having a Threat Null parallel, so as to reflect that the events of the Reckoning, and the effect it had on the Umbra was the sort of cataclysm that VE's basically spent their entire lives anticipating and bracing for. However, I'd be lying if I said that I hadn't contemplated what their version of Threat Null would be, and I almost immediately thought of The Clans from Battletech. From a tonal and thematic standpoint, it made (and still makes) a good amount of sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}